.TH PIPE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
pipe \- create a pipe
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "int pipe(int* " descriptors ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a unidirectional pipe and writes two descriptors to the supplied
two\-element int buffer. Element 0 is the read end and element 1 is the
write end. Both descriptors are initially blocking and do not have
close\-on\-exec set. Close unused ends when they are no longer needed.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or \-1 with
.B errno
set on failure. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH ERRORS
Include
.BR <errno.h> .
Errors include
.BR EFAULT ,
.BR EMFILE ,
and
.BR ENFILE .
Other Linux pipe errors are possible.
.SH NOTES
Writing to a pipe without readers generates
.B SIGPIPE
unless it is ignored or handled; the write can fail with
.BR EPIPE .
Crunch errno is process\-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR read (3crunch),
.BR write (3crunch),
.BR close (3crunch),
.BR pipe (2)
